  "result": "All five tests pass.\n\nI chose Approach B, snapshot state. The spec's required interface only exposes current balances, so a plain id-to-balance mapping meets every requirement with the least code and O(1) reads, while an event log would add machinery for audit or replay features that nothing in the interface or tests asks for.\n\n**What was done**\n\n- Added `ledger/ledger.py` with the two exceptions and the `Ledger` class from the spec. The existing `ledger/__init__.py` was left as is.\n- Amounts are validated as non-negative ints, with `ValueError` for negatives or non-integers. Opening a duplicate account raises `ValueError`, and any reference to a missing account raises `UnknownAccount`.\n- Transfers validate both accounts and the source balance before touching either balance, so a failed transfer leaves state unchanged.\n\n**Verification**\n\n```\npython -m pytest -q\n5 passed in 0.03s\n```\n\nNothing under `tests/` was modified, and no commit was made.",
